front. Awning roof (flat thin box) could cast shadow and enhance.\n- No full roof, so interior readable but maybe look open-air weird. Project Zomboid roof would exist; but top-down needs roof cut. Could add partial roof sections around edges to imply. Add perimeter roof/eaves only (ring) at top, leaving interior open; nice. Use beam boxes around wall tops extending 0.6.\n- Sign above door on porch.\n- Add interior:\n  - floor with rug plane.\n  - shelves/cabinets as containers. \n  - tables/chairs.\n  - counter.\n  - couch.\n  - refrigerator with hum? add.\n  - clutter papers.\n- Colliders for walls, furniture (some).\n- Add point light warm inside if dark? only a couple to avoid performance.\n\nNeed building shape:\n```\nfunction buildBuilding(cfg) {\n group; floor;\n const wallMat...\n // walls four sides: coordinates based on x,z center,w,d\n // For each side, create entries with gap\n```\nSimplify orientation by rotate group? Use all local coordinates and rotation around Y by angle (0 front south, PI/2 front west? complicated). Better build local and set group rotation? Colliders need world transformed. We can instead generate at center with front side defined from 'south','north','east','west'. Use formulas for walls. Build walls individually in world coordinates:\n- define halfW = w/2, halfD=d/2.\n- walls:\n  - north (z=-halfD), full.\n  - south (z=+halfD) if front south with door gap.\n  - west/east full.\n- helper addWall(axis, fixedCoord, from,to, openings?). For wall along x: box(length, H, thickness) at center. For split, segments around gap.\n- door gap width 1.6. Add door frame posts and header.\n- Build colliders for segments.\n- For front east/west similar.\n- Add windows to non-front walls: window panel inside wall with frame; still collider.\n- Garage front large opening for auto shop. Implement `garage:true`: front gap 5.5.\n- Warehouse loading dock door.\n- Add interior partition for house? Optional but visual.\n- Colliders furniture.\n\nChunk dr